Subject: [PATCH 0/2] ASoC: amd: add DMI quirks for Huawei MateBook M1080

The Huawei MateBook D16 with board name "HVY-WXX9" and product version
"M1080" ships the same AMD Renoir ACP block and ES8316 codec as the
MateBook revisions already handled in these two quirk tables (M1010,
M1020, M1040), but its DMI strings match no existing entry.

The result is a board with no analog playback at all. snd_acp_config
never returns FLAG_AMD_LEGACY for it, so the legacy ACP backend is not
selected and the acp3x-es83xx platform device never gets a driver bound.
Only the HDMI codec shows up in aplay -l, and the internal speakers are
silent on every current kernel.

Both tables need an entry, hence two patches. Each adds a single entry
identical in shape to the neighbouring MateBook ones - 22 added lines in
total, changing no behaviour on any other machine, since they take effect
only on an exact three-way DMI match.

With both applied the card comes up as

  card 1: acp3xes83xx [acp3x-es83xx], device 0: ES8316 HiFi-0

and PipeWire exposes a working "Audio Coprocessor Speakers" sink.

The board uses the default 12.288 MHz master clock, so ES83XX_ENABLE_DMIC
alone is correct here; ES83XX_48_MHZ_MCLK produces audible distortion on
this hardware.

Confirmed on two independent M1080 units, both MateBook D16 with a Ryzen 5
4600H (Renoir), reporting identical DMI strings:

  board_vendor    : HUAWEI
  product_name    : HVY-WXX9
  product_version : M1080

The change has been carried out of tree as a DKMS module since May 2026:
https://github.com/azorkai/huawei-matebook-m1080-linux-audio

azorkai (2):
  ASoC: amd: acp-config: add DMI quirk for Huawei MateBook M1080
  ASoC: amd: acp3x-es83xx: add DMI quirk for Huawei MateBook M1080

 sound/soc/amd/acp-config.c                    | 14 ++++++++++++++
 sound/soc/amd/acp/acp3x-es83xx/acp3x-es83xx.c |  8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 22 insertions(+)

